# MHP UI contract

Read `docs/DESIGN.md` completely before visual or component work. It is the
source of truth and overrides generic design preferences.

- Pure white and black foundation: use existing theme tokens; never add beige,
  cream, bronze, brown, gradients, or another accent color. Use the existing
  gold tokens only for primary CTA hover and small uppercase eyebrow labels.
- Minimalist, mildly brutalist, classy: strong rules, editorial type, compact
  spacing, 2px corners, no shadows, no pills.
- Present multiple courses or dates as compact equal-height bordered card
  grids, not oversized full-width rows or long-scroll sections.
- Keep the header in three zones: product navigation, the account control and
  one call to action. Nav items use square chips: grey hover, black fill when
  selected; never underline the brand or nav links for current-page state.
  The account control is a bordered monogram trigger, never a nav chip; signed
  -out visitors get one secondary auth button (Sign in, or Sign up on the
  sign-in page).
- Below `lg`, collapse navigation into the full-height sheet in
  `src/features/site-shell/mobile-menu.tsx` and keep the call to action in the
  bar, outside the menu. Pin account actions to the bottom of the sheet and
  respect `env(safe-area-inset-*)` for installed/standalone windows.
- Set course prices in the functional sans-serif with tabular numbers, never
  the editorial serif.
- Keep the language control as the custom fixed-width dropdown and preserve
  localized equivalent routes. Switching FR/DE/EN must not move surrounding
  controls.
- Make each course card one full-surface link. Primary buttons are black (or
  white on black) and reveal gold only on hover; secondary buttons gain a grey
  surface and never blend into the page.
- Multi-day calendar sessions are one continuous named bar across occupied
  days, with the course name in small sans-serif type on the bar.
- Keep historical course artwork as a compact square thumbnail, visually remove
  its embedded `/` or `//` mark without cropping its title, and never split a
  card into tall image/text columns.
- Undated courses are not sold. Label the schedule as awaiting confirmation
 and send the primary action to a waiting-list form stored in PostgreSQL.
- A course is a `module` or a `programme`. Keep programmes out of the category
 grids: close the catalogue with them under their own rule and heading, as an
 alternative to booking modules one by one. Use the wide inverted-header
 programme card, list the included modules, and show the separate-modules
 total and saving only when the bundle is actually cheaper.
- Animate only clickable encouragement: short black/white inversion, <=2px
  lift, <=4px CTA arrow movement, or pending spinner. No entrance or ambient
  animation.
- Reuse `src/shared/ui` and `src/features/site-shell`; do not make page-specific
  versions of the shell, buttons, or locale switcher. Admin records lead with
  `<BackLink>`: a secondary 44px control back to the list, never a quiet
  underlined “All …” line that can be mistaken for a heading.

- Transactional email is not page HTML. Follow `docs/EMAIL.md` and compose only
  through `composeTransactionalEmail()` in `src/features/email/layout.ts`.
- Before completion, run `pnpm verify` and inspect desktop plus ~390px in FR,
  DE, and EN with no browser/server console errors.
